    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I want a separate RNA-protein partial-correlation network for each of our 10 kidney transplant biopsies with LIONESS-DRAGON, using a 1,000-gene RNA table as layer one; both layers come from the same 10 biopsies with continuous values and no gaps. For layer two there are two protein files, a trimmed 800-protein panel and the full 3,000-protein table. I'm not sure which of those two files my supervisor wants me to use."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before I choose a workflow, please tell me:\n- Do you know which protein file your supervisor wants to use: the trimmed 800-protein panel or the full 3,000-protein table?\n  You wrote: \"I'm not sure which of those two files my supervisor wants me to use\". LIONESS-DRAGON's contract: \"LIONESS-DRAGON consumes exactly two paired sample-by-feature continuous omics tables, DRAGON's inputs, and produces the aggregate DRAGON matrix plus one partial-correlation network per sample, written as an edge-by-sample table (source, target, one column per sample) with layer-qualified node IDs\".\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
